From dd518f028fda536c75abd13971d0fa127aa50664 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 11:23:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] Report through logging, check config.yml, run the tests
 on GitHub

Messages
- every print() of the package goes through the logging module, one logger
  per module under TopoPyScale; shown in the terminal as before by default
- project.verbose: True (default), False (warnings and errors only) or a
  level; project.log_file: outputs/logs/topopyscale_<date>.log by default,
  with time stamps and the Python warnings of the run
- TopoPyScale.log.setup() for use outside Topoclass
- fetch_dem, topo_obs and fetch_era5 no longer switch off warnings for the
  whole session (failed FSM2oshd runs, missing numba... were hidden)

Configuration
- config_reference.yml (the documented example, kept identical by a test)
  lists the keys TopoPyScale reads; Topoclass reports keys of older versions
  with what replaced them, and unknown keys with the closest documented key
  (the examples set project.CPU_cores, which is not read)
- a missing config file raises FileNotFoundError instead of failing later

Cleanup
- ds_param.nc: NaN were packed as ordinary int16 values (a masked cell read
  back as ~2000 m); missing values now get a _FillValue
- sys.exit() in library code replaced by exceptions; bare except replaced
  by the exceptions expected; pdb imports removed
- fetch_dem tile download used undefined names; sim_fsm landform resampling
  (topo_map_forcing) shares the working resampler of topo_map_sim
- mp.to_cryogrid(): the cluster map was never exported ('cluster:labels')
- to_fsm2() raises NotImplementedError instead of failing on undefined names
- fetch_ifs_forecast.py moved to scripts/: it downloads at import

CI: the workflow installs Python 3.13 and runs flake8 (syntax errors and
undefined names, now none) and the test suite on every push and pull
request, instead of an example on commits tagged [trigger test] with 3.9.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012FMkEYDUJxvxmd3SbUsJfP
